load @term/seed/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# A linear combination: a sum of vectors each scaled by a scalar, the basic operation of a vector space, from which span,
# basis, and dimension are defined. Every vector in a space is a linear combination of a basis. The twenty-four
# directions of the 24-cell are the integer linear combinations that land on its vertices. The form carries the vector
# space the combination is formed in.
form linear-combination
  link space, like vector-space
